  "question": {
    "text": "Four identical point masses, each of mass $\\mathrm{m}$ and carrying charge $+\\mathrm{q}$ are placed at the corners of a square of sides 'a' on a frictionless plain surface. If the particles are released simultaneously, the kinetic energy of the system when they are infinitely far apart is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{q^{2}}{a}(2 \\sqrt{2}+1) \\times \\mathrm{k}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}}(\\sqrt{2}+2) \\times \\mathrm{k}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{q^{2}}{a}(\\sqrt{2}+4) \\times \\mathrm{k}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{q^{2}}{a}(\\sqrt{2}+1) \\times \\mathrm{k}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\nHint $: \\mathrm{KE}_{i}+\\mathrm{PE}_{\\mathrm{i}}=\\mathrm{KE}_{\\mathrm{f}}+\\mathrm{PE}_{\\mathrm{f}}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{KE}_{\\mathrm{t}}=\\mathrm{PE}_{i}=4 \\frac{\\mathrm{Kq}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}}+2 \\frac{\\mathrm{Kq}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Kq}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}}(4+\\sqrt{2}), \\mathrm{K}=1$ in C.G.S. unit"
  }
}